//Shadowing contract (builtin-decls source-of-truth spec 6.8): a user
//class named like a prelude builtin wins at EVERY site — type position,
//construction, and member access. Before the Semaphore cluster
//migrates, the constructor-call site short-circuits to the synthesized
//builtin singleton (whose ctor requires one int), so this program fails
//to compile; after the migration it returns the user field's value.
class Semaphore {
    public int tag;
    public Semaphore() {
        tag = 7;
    }
}

int main() {
    Semaphore s = Semaphore();
    return s.tag;
}
